# CMake and IDE build output -- the GENERAL forms, not a list of names.
#
# This file named build directories one at a time, and a new one was always one
# build ahead of the list. Two consequences, both measured:
#
#   * build_phase5/ and build_vst3/ sat in this repo's history until QBX-132
#     untracked them: generated files, committed because nothing covered them
#     at the time they first appeared.
#   * MangroveIPlug/build-mac/ was never named, though its build-win/ sibling
#     was. 210 of its 314 files matched no rule at all, so `git add -A` would
#     have staged 138 MB of build output.
#
# The per-file rules below (*.o, *.a, *.dylib) are NOT a substitute. They cover
# a build tree only incidentally and miss generated sources, CMake internals
# and ninja state. qbx carries these same two patterns after the same leak
# (qbx#220); ci/gates.sh's build-ci/ and build-ci-plugin/ are covered here too.
#
# The trailing slash is load-bearing: it matches directories only, so a FILE
# named build-* stays tracked -- including
# external/iplug2/Dependencies/build-skia-mac.sh, which the last line of this
# file un-ignores on purpose.
build/
build-*/
build_*/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
.DS_Store

# Windows / Visual Studio output. The build-win/ directories under
# MangrovePlugin/ and MangroveIPlug/ are covered by build-*/ above: a pattern
# with no leading slash matches at any depth.
*.log
.vs/

# Skia build artifacts (large binaries, not checked in)
external/iplug2/Dependencies/Build/
!external/iplug2/Dependencies/build-skia-mac.sh
